 "subs": [
  {
   "a": 0.1,
   "b": 4.2,
   "zh": "如果现在就为未来的自己投资，",
   "en": "If you were going to invest now in your future best self,",
   "kind": "clip"
  },
  {
   "a": 4.9,
   "b": 7.8,
   "zh": "你会把时间和精力放在哪里？",
   "en": "where would you put your time and your energy?",
   "kind": "clip"
  },
  {
   "a": 8.36,
   "b": 11.62,
   "zh": "这是 TED 上被看了五千多万次的一场演讲",
   "kind": "nar"
  },
  {
   "a": 12.144,
   "b": 13.802,
   "zh": "讲的人叫 Robert Waldinger",
   "kind": "nar"
  },
  {
   "a": 13.852,
   "b": 15.844,
   "zh": "哈佛医学院的精神科教授",
   "kind": "nar"
  },
  {
   "a": 16.368,
   "b": 17.932,
   "zh": "他手里有一项研究",
   "kind": "nar"
  },
  {
   "a": 17.982,
   "b": 19.546,
   "zh": "从一九三八年开始",
   "kind": "nar"
  },
  {
   "a": 19.596,
   "b": 20.958,
   "zh": "一直做到了今天",
   "kind": "nar"
  },
  {
   "a": 21.563,
   "b": 28.463,
   "zh": "哈佛成人发展研究，可能是同类研究里做得最久的一项。",
   "en": "The Harvard Study of Adult Development may be the longest study of adult life ever done.",
   "kind": "clip"
  },
  {
   "a": 29.563,
   "b": 35.763,
   "zh": "75 年里，我们跟踪了 724 位男性的一生。",
   "en": "For 75 years, we've tracked the lives of 724 men.",
   "kind": "clip"
  },
  {
   "a": 36.333,
   "b": 38.023,
   "zh": "七百多个人，分成两组",
   "kind": "nar"
  },
  {
   "a": 38.603,
   "b": 40.283,
   "zh": "一组是哈佛的大二学生",
   "kind": "nar"
  },
  {
   "a": 40.853,
   "b": 43.613,
   "zh": "另一组，是波士顿最穷街区的男孩",
   "kind": "nar"
  },
  {
   "a": 44.223,
   "b": 46.403,
   "zh": "每隔两年，研究者就上门一次",
   "kind": "nar"
  },
  {
   "a": 46.453,
   "b": 48.633,
   "zh": "问卷、病历、抽血、扫描大脑",
   "kind": "nar"
  },
  {
   "a": 49.203,
   "b": 51.813,
   "zh": "一跟，就跟到了他们九十多岁",
   "kind": "nar"
  },
  {
   "a": 52.35,
   "b": 54.14,
   "zh": "七十五年，几万页记录",
   "kind": "nar"
  },
  {
   "a": 54.89,
   "b": 57.66,
   "zh": "最后能说清楚的，只有一句话",
   "kind": "nar"
  },
  {
   "a": 58.267,
   "b": 64.167,
   "zh": "结论跟财富、名望、更拼命工作都没有关系。",
   "en": "The lessons aren't about wealth or fame or working harder and harder.",
   "kind": "clip"
  },
  {
   "a": 65.067,
   "b": 70.667,
   "zh": "这项 75 年的研究，给出的最明确的一条是：",
   "en": "The clearest message that we get from this 75-year study is this:",
   "kind": "clip"
  },
  {
   "a": 71.667,
   "b": 76.767,
   "zh": "好的关系让人更快乐、更健康。就这样。",
   "en": "Good relationships keep us happier and healthier. Period.",
   "kind": "clip"
  },
  {
   "a": 77.767,
   "b": 82.467,
   "zh": "人可以在人群中孤独，也可以在婚姻里孤独。",
   "en": "And we know that you can be lonely in a crowd and you can be lonely in a marriage.",
   "kind": "clip"
  },
  {
   "a": 83.467,
   "b": 88.367,
   "zh": "所以第二条结论是：不只看你有多少朋友，",
   "en": "So the second big lesson is that it's not just the number of friends you have,",
   "kind": "clip"
  },
  {
   "a": 88.767,
   "b": 91.667,
   "zh": "也不只看你有没有伴侣，",
   "en": "and it's not whether or not you're in a committed relationship,",
   "kind": "clip"
  },
  {
   "a": 91.767,
   "b": 96.567,
   "zh": "真正要紧的，是亲密关系的质量。",
   "en": "but it's the quality of your close relationships that matters.",
   "kind": "clip"
  },
  {
   "a": 97.137,
   "b": 98.817,
   "zh": "他把这句话拆成三层",
   "kind": "nar"
  },
  {
   "a": 99.607,
   "b": 101.557,
   "zh": "第一层，孤独伤的是身体",
   "kind": "nar"
  },
  {
   "a": 102.327,
   "b": 104.987,
   "zh": "第二层，五十岁，就能预测八十岁",
   "kind": "nar"
  },
  {
   "a": 105.717,
   "b": 108.817,
   "zh": "第三层，靠得住的人，护住的是大脑",
   "kind": "nar"
  },
  {
   "a": 109.494,
   "b": 110.984,
   "zh": "先看孤独的那一头",
   "kind": "nar"
  },
  {
   "a": 111.584,
   "b": 115.384,
   "zh": "第一，跟人有连接，对我们真的有好处；",
   "en": "The first is that social connections are really good for us,",
   "kind": "clip"
  },
  {
   "a": 115.484,
   "b": 117.284,
   "zh": "而孤独会要人命。",
   "en": "and that loneliness kills.",
   "kind": "clip"
  },
  {
   "a": 117.484,
   "b": 121.684,
   "zh": "那些比自己希望的更孤立的人，",
   "en": "People who are more isolated than they want to be from others",
   "kind": "clip"
  },
  {
   "a": 122.484,
   "b": 125.184,
   "zh": "没那么快乐，",
   "en": "find that they are less happy,",
   "kind": "clip"
  },
  {
   "a": 126.084,
   "b": 128.584,
   "zh": "中年时健康更早开始下滑，",
   "en": "their health declines earlier in midlife,",
   "kind": "clip"
  },
  {
   "a": 129.084,
   "b": 131.084,
   "zh": "大脑功能衰退得更早，",
   "en": "their brain functioning declines sooner",
   "kind": "clip"
  },
  {
   "a": 131.184,
   "b": 134.784,
   "zh": "寿命也比不孤独的人短。",
   "en": "and they live shorter lives than people who are not lonely.",
   "kind": "clip"
  },
  {
   "a": 135.364,
   "b": 137.034,
   "zh": "孤独不只是一种心情",
   "kind": "nar"
  },
  {
   "a": 137.684,
   "b": 140.194,
   "zh": "身体和大脑，都会提前衰老",
   "kind": "nar"
  },
  {
   "a": 140.868,
   "b": 143.818,
   "zh": "等这批人活到八十多岁，研究者做了一件事",
   "kind": "nar"
  },
  {
   "a": 144.388,
   "b": 147.559,
   "zh": "他们翻出每个人五十岁时的全部记录",
   "kind": "nar"
  },
  {
   "a": 147.609,
   "b": 149.169,
   "zh": "想找出到底哪一项",
   "kind": "nar"
  },
  {
   "a": 149.219,
   "b": 150.578,
   "zh": "能提前预测晚年",
   "kind": "nar"
  },
  {
   "a": 151.183,
   "b": 156.383,
   "zh": "把他们 50 岁时的所有资料放在一起看，",
   "en": "When we gathered together everything we knew about them at age 50,",
   "kind": "clip"
  },
  {
   "a": 157.383,
   "b": 162.283,
   "zh": "预测他们怎样变老的，不是中年的胆固醇水平，",
   "en": "it wasn't their middle-age cholesterol levels that predicted how they were going to grow old.",
   "kind": "clip"
  },
  {
   "a": 162.983,
   "b": 166.283,
   "zh": "是他们对自己的关系有多满意。",
   "en": "It was how satisfied they were in their relationships.",
   "kind": "clip"
  },
  {
   "a": 166.483,
   "b": 174.183,
   "zh": "50 岁时对关系最满意的人，80 岁时最健康。",
   "en": "The people most satisfied in their relationships at age 50 were the healthiest at age 80.",
   "kind": "clip"
  },
  {
   "a": 174.733,
   "b": 178.773,
   "zh": "五十岁时关系好不好，比胆固醇，更能预测八十岁",
   "kind": "nar"
  },
  {
   "a": 179.447,
   "b": 180.987,
   "zh": "第三层，在大脑里",
   "kind": "nar"
  },
  {
   "a": 181.491,
   "b": 189.791,
   "zh": "80 多岁时，有一段让人安心的关系，是一种保护。",
   "en": "Being in a securely attached relationship to another person in your 80s is protective.",
   "kind": "clip"
  },
  {
   "a": 189.991,
   "b": 195.991,
   "zh": "真心觉得需要的时候能指望对方的人，",
   "en": "People who really feel they can count on the other person in times of need,",
   "kind": "clip"
  },
  {
   "a": 196.191,
   "b": 198.891,
   "zh": "记忆力保持清晰的时间更长。",
   "en": "those people's memories stay sharper longer.",
   "kind": "clip"
  },
  {
   "a": 199.461,
   "b": 201.261,
   "zh": "好的关系，不等于从不吵架",
   "kind": "nar"
  },
  {
   "a": 201.821,
   "b": 203.931,
   "zh": "有些八十多岁的夫妻，天天拌嘴",
   "kind": "nar"
  },
  {
   "a": 204.531,
   "b": 209.111,
   "zh": "可只要相信关键时刻对方靠得住，记忆就不受影响",
   "kind": "nar"
  },
  {
   "a": 209.634,
   "b": 210.994,
   "zh": "吵不吵架不要紧",
   "kind": "nar"
  },
  {
   "a": 211.774,
   "b": 214.354,
   "zh": "难的时候有人靠得住，才要紧",
   "kind": "nar"
  },
  {
   "a": 215.032,
   "b": 216.352,
   "zh": "他给的办法，都很小",
   "kind": "nar"
  },
  {
   "a": 216.958,
   "b": 222.258,
   "zh": "可以简单到把看屏幕的时间，换成跟人在一起；",
   "en": "It might be something as simple as replacing screen time with people time,",
   "kind": "clip"
  },
  {
   "a": 223.558,
   "b": 229.658,
   "zh": "或者一起做点新鲜事，散步、约会，让关系重新活起来；",
   "en": "or livening up a stale relationship by doing something new together, long walks or date nights,",
   "kind": "clip"
  },
  {
   "a": 230.458,
   "b": 235.258,
   "zh": "或者联系那位多年没说话的家人。",
   "en": "or reaching out to that family member who you haven't spoken to in years.",
   "kind": "clip"
  },
  {
   "a": 235.828,
   "b": 238.588,
   "zh": "他说，别跟屏幕聊天，去跟人聊天",
   "kind": "nar"
  },
  {
   "a": 239.188,
   "b": 239.855,
   "zh": "十年过去",
   "kind": "nar"
  },
  {
   "a": 239.905,
   "b": 242.005,
   "zh": "很多人每天聊得最多的对象",
   "kind": "nar"
  },
  {
   "a": 242.055,
   "b": 243.008,
   "zh": "变成了 AI",
   "kind": "nar"
  },
  {
   "a": 243.568,
   "b": 246.188,
   "zh": "能交给 AI 的事，都交出去",
   "kind": "nar"
  },
  {
   "a": 246.898,
   "b": 249.728,
   "zh": "省下来的时间，留给靠得住的人",
   "kind": "nar"
  }
 ],
